<section class="surface section" id="how-it-works"><div class="wrap">
  <p class="eyebrow">A familiar workflow</p><h2>From your editor to your inbox.</h2>
  <div class="three-grid steps"><article><span class="step-number">01</span><div><h3>Create a draft with your assistant.</h3><p>Use the supported local Codex client to prepare a form for your site. Review its schema and integration code.</p></div></article><article><span class="step-number">02</span><div><h3>Review and publish.</h3><p>Check the fields and allowed origin. Explicitly approve the exact form and version before publication.</p></div></article><article><span class="step-number">03</span><div><h3>Collect responses across your sites.</h3><p>Open your authorized submissions dashboard to inspect accepted responses and their site and form.</p></div></article></div>
</div></section>
<section class="section wrap"><div class="three-grid benefits">
  <article><span class="line-icon" aria-hidden="true">&lt;/&gt;</span><h2>Your site stays yours.</h2><p>GoFormX works with your site's frontend. Keep control of your code, stack and hosting.</p></article>
  <article><span class="line-icon" aria-hidden="true">▤</span><h2>Your forms stay together.</h2><p>Manage forms and review authorized responses in one place, grouped by site and form.</p></article>
  <article><span class="line-icon" aria-hidden="true">◇</span><h2>You decide what your assistant can access.</h2><p>GoFormX grants control what an assistant may manage. Reading submission content requires a separate permission.</p></article>
</div></section>
<section class="surface section"><div class="wrap proof-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">A working example</p><h2>Already collecting real enquiries.</h2><p>The contact form on Russell Jones's personal site delivers submissions to GoFormX. Live browser acceptance and inbox receipt were verified on September 30, 2026.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://jonesrussell.github.io/me/contact">See the working example <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="small">The link opens the site. Please do not send test enquiries.</p></div><div class="receipt panel" aria-label="Illustrative acceptance receipt"><p class="micro">Illustration · synthetic receipt</p><span class="receipt-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><h3>Submission accepted</h3><dl><div><dt>Form</dt><dd>Contact</dd></div><div><dt>Site</dt><dd>Example portfolio</dd></div><div><dt>Schema</dt><dd>Version 1</dd></div></dl><p class="small">Inbox receipt is separate from email delivery.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section wrap"><h2>Starting with Codex. Built toward more.</h2><div class="two-grid compatibility-cards"><article><span class="line-icon terminal" aria-hidden="true">&gt;_</span><div><h3>Codex: local workflow verified</h3><p>The API/script client completed a local two-site journey. Live personal-site capture was verified separately.</p><a class="text-link" href="/compatibility">Read the evidence and limits <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></article><article><span class="line-icon" aria-hidden="true">◌</span><div><h3>Other assistants: planned</h3><p>Hermes, ChatGPT and Claude are intended targets. Their connection paths have not yet been verified.</p></div></article></div></section>
<section class="surface section"><div class="wrap"><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="three-grid faq"><article><h3>Do submissions require AI?</h3><p>No. AI helps manage forms; collection runs independently of model calls.</p></article><article><h3>Is the inbox email?</h3><p>No. It is your submissions dashboard. Authorized owners and admins can inspect received data.</p></article><article><h3>Are email notifications available?</h3><p>Email notification delivery is not yet verified. Do not rely on it as your receipt channel.</p></article></div></div></section>
